+The non-Error rejection behaviour remains outside issue #93.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Turn usage — issue #93
+
+The chosen contract keeps one usage argument and sums its token fields across provider calls; a per-round breakdown is rejected because billing and budgeting need a turn total and do not require a wider public surface ([validated by: sums all three token fields when both values are defined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L33)). The public hook signature must name the value as total turn usage, and the MINOR release changelog must explain that existing consumers record larger numbers for tool-heavy turns ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call after two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/usage.acceptance.test.ts#L57)).
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once after the loop and receives the sum of input, output and total tokens from every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final answer ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call after two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/usage.acceptance.test.ts#L57)).
+- Missing usage in any round is ignored while summing reported rounds; when no round reports usage the hook still receives `undefined` ([validated by: sums reported rounds despite missing usage and preserves an entirely unreported turn](../../src/orchestration/usage.acceptance.test.ts#L67) [validated by: returns the defined value when the accumulator is absent](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L38) [validated by: returns the accumulator when the next value is absent](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L43) [validated by: returns undefined when both values are absent](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L48)).
+- A turn without tools retains its existing response text and usage values ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
